00:13:10,874 --> 00:13:12,375
I think
he kinda likes the pain.

257
00:13:14,878 --> 00:13:17,589
I admire the way
you stood up for Flanagan.

258
00:13:17,631 --> 00:13:18,590
It pissed me off...

259
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,427
...but I understand.

260
00:13:23,553 --> 00:13:25,347
You know, a man gets to be
my age, you start thinking

261
00:13:25,388 --> 00:13:26,598
about certain things.

262
00:13:29,518 --> 00:13:31,561
Do I care about
this award? No.

263
00:13:32,604 --> 00:13:35,398
But it does symbolize
something important.

264
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:36,525
And that's,

265
00:13:36,566 --> 00:13:38,276
you sum up a man's life,

266
00:13:38,318 --> 00:13:40,570
you want to know
what he stood for, right?

267
00:13:41,613 --> 00:13:44,533
Now, I don't give half a shit
about the Hibernian Society,

268
00:13:44,574 --> 00:13:47,202
but I care about
this neighborhood.

269
00:13:50,914 --> 00:13:52,457
So, what'd you want
to come see me about?

270
00:13:54,543 --> 00:13:58,713
That Starship job
Castellano gave us.

271
00:13:58,755 --> 00:14:00,924
Look, I know you share
his feelings about dealing coke

272
00:14:00,966 --> 00:14:02,425
and I get it.

273
00:14:02,467 --> 00:14:03,927
I do...

274
00:14:04,886 --> 00:14:07,097
but if we don't deal it,
someone else will.

275
00:14:07,138 --> 00:14:09,224
I mean, they already are,

276
00:14:09,266 --> 00:14:10,976
and whoever does,

277
00:14:11,017 --> 00:14:13,562
they'll just become stronger
and more of a threat to us.

278
00:14:13,603 --> 00:14:15,855
Why are we having
this conversation, Jimmy?

279
00:14:18,024 --> 00:14:19,943
Because I took six kilos
from that disco

280
00:14:19,985 --> 00:14:21,152
before we burned it down.

281
00:14:23,071 --> 00:14:26,408
Fuck! Jesus Christ.
Zip that shit up.

282
00:14:26,449 --> 00:14:27,742
Goddamnit!

283
00:14:29,119 --> 00:14:31,204
Look, we could use the money
to help Pat's ma and his kid.

284
00:14:31,246 --> 00:14:32,747
If it even is
his fucking kid.

285
00:14:32,789 --> 00:14:34,874
To be frank with you, Eamon,

286
00:14:34,915 --> 00:14:36,042
you know, you're giving
all this money away

287
00:14:36,084 --> 00:14:38,587
to charity,
which is great,

288
00:14:38,628 --> 00:14:41,047
but me and the boys are
kinda hurtin' for cash.

289
00:14:41,089 --> 00:14:43,383
And this...
this Javits Center is

290
00:14:43,425 --> 00:14:45,051
all well and good
for you but--

291
00:14:45,093 --> 00:14:47,345
This Javits Center is gonna
help all of us, okay?

292
00:14:47,387 --> 00:14:48,930
-It's bringing in millions--
-Yeah, no, I know--

293
00:14:48,972 --> 00:14:52,225
Unless-- Unless
you fuck it up dealing drugs.

294
00:14:55,228 --> 00:14:57,772
The Feds are handing out
30-year sentences for narcotics.

295
00:14:58,898 --> 00:15:00,650
So, somebody gets busted,

296
00:15:00,692 --> 00:15:01,985
they're gonna fucking flip.

297
00:15:03,945 --> 00:15:06,698
That's why Big Paul is
against it and I am too.

298
00:15:06,740 --> 00:15:08,783
With all due respect, Eamon,

299
00:15:08,825 --> 00:15:10,952
you can't stop cocaine
from taking over.

300
00:15:10,994 --> 00:15:12,746
Demand's too great.

301
00:15:12,787 --> 00:15:15,540
And I think
it's worth the risk.

302
00:15:16,583 --> 00:15:19,586
You fucking shot Zaccaro
against my wishes,

303
00:15:19,628 --> 00:15:21,588
and good riddance,
fuck that guy.

304
00:15:21,630 --> 00:15:23,965
We're still trying to clean up
that fucking mess, okay?

305
00:15:24,007 --> 00:15:25,592
Don't go against me on this.

306
00:15:25,634 --> 00:15:26,968
I'm gonna fuckin' burn
this shit.

307
00:15:27,010 --> 00:15:28,178
-But I'm just-- I--
-Look, we don't

308
00:15:28,219 --> 00:15:30,013
fucking deal drugs.

309
00:15:30,055 --> 00:15:31,640
Period. Understood?

310
00:15:33,391 --> 00:15:34,643
Yes, sir.

311
00:15:37,604 --> 00:15:39,272
Make sure your crew
gets that message.

312
00:15:41,775 --> 00:15:45,528
[Italian music playing on radio]

313
00:15:47,614 --> 00:15:49,574
I've been leaning
on the Dominicans

314
00:15:49,616 --> 00:15:50,909
and the Harlem crews.

315
00:15:50,950 --> 00:15:52,744
Everybody knows
something went down...

316
00:15:53,703 --> 00:15:55,747
but nobody knows
who stole your cocaine.

317
00:15:55,789 --> 00:15:58,458
We need fucking answers.

318
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:00,669
You tell every corner boy
from Jamaica to Jerome

319
00:16:00,710 --> 00:16:02,587
that if so much as
a gram of my coke shows up,

320
00:16:02,629 --> 00:16:04,923
I want to know where, when,
and who's holding it.

321
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:06,716
-Absolutely.
-And you let them know that

322
00:16:06,758 --> 00:16:08,843
any stupid motherfucker
caught trying to sell

323
00:16:08,885 --> 00:16:10,804
my product,
they're gonna die.

324
00:16:10,845 --> 00:16:12,305
I understand.

325
00:16:12,347 --> 00:16:14,474
Whoever fucking robbed you

326
00:16:14,516 --> 00:16:15,767
knew to use
Zaccaro's name.

327
00:16:15,809 --> 00:16:17,352
So, if you ask me,
it's Big Paul,

328
00:16:17,394 --> 00:16:18,812
sending a message
through the back door,

329
00:16:18,853 --> 00:16:21,189
and using those fuckin'
Micks as pawns.

330
00:16:21,231 --> 00:16:23,817
-Backstabbing cocksucker.
-He's got brass fucking balls.

331
00:16:23,858 --> 00:16:25,485
Yeah.

332
00:16:25,527 --> 00:16:27,404
One day, I'm gonna
shove them up his ass.

333
00:16:29,030 --> 00:16:30,532
Now, fuck off.

334
00:16:33,618 --> 00:16:37,038
[tense music]

335
00:16:53,221 --> 00:16:54,597
[knocking on door]

336
00:17:01,229 --> 00:17:03,356
Hello, Moira.

337
00:17:03,398 --> 00:17:05,525
What the hell
are you doing here?

338
00:17:05,567 --> 00:17:08,486
I need to talk to Danny.
He here?

339
00:17:08,528 --> 00:17:09,404
He's in school.

340
00:17:11,156 --> 00:17:12,365
School?

341
00:17:12,406 --> 00:17:15,285
Yeah. That's what
he tells me anyway.

342
00:17:17,036 --> 00:17:18,496
When will he be home?

343
00:17:20,205 --> 00:17:22,333
No idea.

344
00:17:22,375 --> 00:17:24,919
But he won't want to see you,
I can tell ya that right now.

345
00:17:24,961 --> 00:17:26,045
Okay.

346
00:17:27,630 --> 00:17:29,299
Can we talk, please?

347
00:17:29,340 --> 00:17:32,051
It's been a long time.
Please? It's important.

348
00:17:33,762 --> 00:17:35,346
Five minutes.

349
00:17:49,319 --> 00:17:52,071
Jacob's Biscuits?
Where'd you find those?

350
00:17:52,113 --> 00:17:54,866
There's a place on 23rd Street.
Danny picks 'em up for me.

351
00:17:56,659 --> 00:17:58,870
So he says
he's going to school?

352
00:17:58,912 --> 00:18:00,288
He's not.
He's hanging out

353
00:18:00,330 --> 00:18:02,415
with Irish gangsters
on the West Side.

354
00:18:03,374 --> 00:18:05,543
To be honest, I don't know
where the hell he goes.

355
00:18:06,377 --> 00:18:08,421
He came back last week
with his face busted up,

356
00:18:08,463 --> 00:18:10,006
and he wouldn't tell me
what happened.

357
00:18:11,591 --> 00:18:13,176
He barely says
a word to me, but...

358
00:18:14,135 --> 00:18:16,554
he buys me these biscuits
'cause he knows that I like 'em.

359
00:18:19,808 --> 00:18:21,351
And Eileen liked them too.

360
00:18:21,392 --> 00:18:23,853
Yeah. They were her favorite.

361
00:18:27,357 --> 00:18:28,900
So, I been trying.

362
00:18:28,942 --> 00:18:31,778
I've been trying to form

363
00:18:31,820 --> 00:18:34,364
some kind of
a relationship with him.

364
00:18:34,405 --> 00:18:36,908
It's a bit late for that.

365
00:18:36,950 --> 00:18:39,911
Yeah, well,
maybe you could help me.

366
00:18:39,953 --> 00:18:41,871
How could I help you?

367
00:18:41,913 --> 00:18:43,748
You know, better question,

368
00:18:43,790 --> 00:18:46,709
why the fuck should I help you?

369
00:18:46,751 --> 00:18:48,461
I haven't seen you
since my sister's funeral.

370
00:18:50,922 --> 00:18:53,842
You think it's been
a pleasure raising that boy?

371
00:18:53,883 --> 00:18:56,845
Every birthday, Christmas...

372
00:18:58,012 --> 00:19:00,473
every anniversary
of my sister's death, and...

373
00:19:01,891 --> 00:19:03,309
...not a fucking peep
out of you.

374
00:19:05,478 --> 00:19:06,855
I can't change that.

375
00:19:09,649 --> 00:19:11,150
Let me try and fix things.

376
00:19:11,192 --> 00:19:12,402
Right.

377
00:19:15,196 --> 00:19:16,114
[door shutting]

378
00:19:19,075 --> 00:19:20,493
[sighs]

379
00:19:21,369 --> 00:19:23,037
Look who came by
to say hello.

380
00:19:31,629 --> 00:19:33,715
-[Sweeney] Look at this shit.
-[Breen] What the fuck?

381
00:19:33,756 --> 00:19:35,925
Right? So, if this is pure,
it's gotta be worth,

382
00:19:35,967 --> 00:19:37,468
I don't know,
three, four hundred grand...

383
00:19:38,678 --> 00:19:40,847
a lot of fuckin' money.

384
00:19:40,889 --> 00:19:42,390
I thought you told Jimmy
that we weren't gonna--

385
00:19:42,432 --> 00:19:45,101
Yeah, if the young guys
start selling this shit,

386
00:19:45,143 --> 00:19:47,562
it's gonna go
tits up for sure.

387
00:19:47,604 --> 00:19:48,980
This is one time only.

388
00:19:54,569 --> 00:19:56,404
And what if
Castellano finds out?

389
00:19:56,446 --> 00:19:57,947
Fuck Big Paul.

390
00:19:57,989 --> 00:19:59,657
He's a hypocrite.

391
00:19:59,699 --> 00:20:01,159
He gets kick-ups
on the same drugs

392
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,952
he forbids Gotti
from selling.

393
00:20:02,994 --> 00:20:05,872
I guess that makes us
hypocrites then, doesn't it?

394
00:20:05,914 --> 00:20:07,665
[exhales]

395
00:20:07,707 --> 00:20:09,584
Yeah, I guess it does.

396
00:20:09,626 --> 00:20:12,420
Maybe I'll donate mine
to the Hibernian Society,

397
00:20:12,462 --> 00:20:13,546
feed the poor Irish.

398
00:20:15,423 --> 00:20:16,674
What are you gonna do
with the rest?

399
00:20:18,885 --> 00:20:20,303
Don't worry, Eddie,
you'll get your cut.

400
00:20:20,345 --> 00:20:21,512
Yeah.

401
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:25,767
Get a hold of Leon, will ya?

402
00:20:26,809 --> 00:20:27,936
Tell him I wanna see him.

403
00:20:30,146 --> 00:20:31,230
Okay.

404
00:20:37,070 --> 00:20:37,946
[door shutting]

405
00:20:47,163 --> 00:20:48,206
[Glenn] Hey.

406
00:21:00,009 --> 00:21:01,594
I owe you an apology.

407
00:21:03,054 --> 00:21:04,305
More than one.

408
00:21:05,765 --> 00:21:06,683
Let me see your face.

409
00:21:14,983 --> 00:21:17,360
You know, my old man used
to hit me a lot growing up.

410
00:21:17,402 --> 00:21:18,695
That's not an excuse.

411
00:21:19,904 --> 00:21:21,572
It's just all I know.

412
00:21:22,532 --> 00:21:24,409
I'll let you in
on a little secret.

413
00:21:25,326 --> 00:21:27,829
I hate myself more
than you could ever hate me.

414
00:21:31,708 --> 00:21:33,334
I'm sorry, Danny.

415
00:21:46,347 --> 00:21:49,517
What I just don't understand is,
why'd you leave?

416
00:21:52,020 --> 00:21:54,188
When your mother
and I got together,

417
00:21:54,230 --> 00:21:56,482
I-- I'd just come back
home from the war.

418
00:21:58,443 --> 00:22:00,737
I-I-I was broken.

419
00:22:02,822 --> 00:22:04,866
I think she was
a little broken, too.

420
00:22:06,034 --> 00:22:08,077
Both of us were drinking hard,

421
00:22:08,119 --> 00:22:10,079
and she got into drugs.

422
00:22:10,121 --> 00:22:11,289
Heroin.

423
00:22:13,291 --> 00:22:14,709
I left.

424
00:22:14,751 --> 00:22:16,085
I fucking left.

425
00:22:18,004 --> 00:22:20,882
I left you behind
with her fuckin' sister,

426
00:22:20,923 --> 00:22:22,925
and I hate myself
for doing that.

427
00:22:24,469 --> 00:22:25,970
But you are my son.

428
00:22:28,890 --> 00:22:30,767
And I love you
with all that I am.

429
00:22:33,728 --> 00:22:36,105
And I would do anything
to protect you from harm.

430
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:42,278
Do you understand that?

431
00:22:49,285 --> 00:22:50,411
Did you kill Pat?

432
00:22:53,623 --> 00:22:54,665
No.

433
00:22:56,834 --> 00:22:59,087
Homicide guys said
it was...

434
00:22:59,128 --> 00:23:01,255
some spics did it
over a dope deal.

435
00:23:03,091 --> 00:23:05,259
This is why I'm sayin'
stay off the streets,

436
00:23:05,301 --> 00:23:06,761
do your schoolwork.

437
00:23:06,803 --> 00:23:08,012
Be good.

438
00:23:09,305 --> 00:23:10,765
Don't end up like Pat.

439
00:23:15,144 --> 00:23:16,354
I'm tired.

440
00:23:20,358 --> 00:23:21,400
[Glenn] All right.

441
00:23:26,989 --> 00:23:28,950
It's okay I come back,
visit you again sometime?

442
00:23:38,126 --> 00:23:41,129
[rock music playing
on headphones]

443
00:23:49,720 --> 00:23:52,515
What's the soonest we can safely
move that package off the docks?

444
00:23:55,560 --> 00:23:57,812
That's why I, uh,
asked you here.

445
00:23:59,021 --> 00:24:00,064
What is it?

446
00:24:02,024 --> 00:24:03,734
I went to check on it
last night,

447
00:24:03,776 --> 00:24:05,236
and it was missing.

448
00:24:05,278 --> 00:24:07,905
And sometimes they clear out
the unused cargo crates,

449
00:24:07,947 --> 00:24:09,949
unbeknownst to me,

450
00:24:09,991 --> 00:24:11,784
and that is probably
what happened.

451
00:24:11,826 --> 00:24:13,870
Are you fuckin' jokin' me?

452
00:24:13,911 --> 00:24:15,371
[Bridget] I'm sorry, Brendan.

453
00:24:15,413 --> 00:24:17,206
It's gone, and it's
probably in a landfill,

454
00:24:17,248 --> 00:24:20,001
which is good 'cause it means
it won't be discovered,

455
00:24:20,042 --> 00:24:21,586
and it will not be
traced back--

456
00:24:24,172 --> 00:24:25,339
[bartender]
Need a hand, Bridget?

457
00:24:27,258 --> 00:24:28,342
Yeah, best not to make a scene.

458
00:24:28,384 --> 00:24:30,761
Is that why
you brought me here?

459
00:24:30,803 --> 00:24:32,847
What'd you think I was gonna do?
Put a fuckin' gun in your mouth?

460
00:24:32,889 --> 00:24:34,223
'Cause you're right.
That's exactly

461
00:24:34,265 --> 00:24:35,474
what I fuckin'
would have done.

462
00:24:35,516 --> 00:24:37,685
Yeah. I wouldn't
put it past ya.

463
00:24:38,853 --> 00:24:41,189
Do you realize
what a major fuck-up this is?

464
00:24:41,230 --> 00:24:42,565
Well, I don't know
what your plan is,

465
00:24:42,607 --> 00:24:43,649
but I'm sure
you'll figure a way around it.

466
00:24:43,691 --> 00:24:45,359
[scoffs]

467
00:24:45,401 --> 00:24:46,652
You're some
piece of work, aren't you?

468
00:24:48,154 --> 00:24:50,198
What I was doing wasn't
just for Ireland.

469
00:24:51,532 --> 00:24:52,700
It was for you.

470
00:24:52,742 --> 00:24:54,410
What're you talking about?

471
00:24:54,452 --> 00:24:55,912
[Brendan]
My target.

472
00:24:55,953 --> 00:24:57,371
The British operative,

473
00:24:57,413 --> 00:24:59,290
flying into New York
from Belfast.

474
00:24:59,332 --> 00:25:00,833
Colonel Gerald Markham.

475
00:25:02,501 --> 00:25:04,212
The man who killed
your parents.

476
00:25:15,890 --> 00:25:18,017
Can't believe we're back
to this nickel-and-dime shit.

477
00:25:19,101 --> 00:25:20,895
Yeah, business as usual.

478
00:25:20,937 --> 00:25:22,563
It's fucked up.

479
00:25:22,605 --> 00:25:24,148
I mean, that coke could
be worth 300 grand,

480
00:25:24,190 --> 00:25:26,234
that's before we even cut it.

481
00:25:26,275 --> 00:25:27,735
A lot of us could use
that kind of fuckin' money.

482
00:25:27,777 --> 00:25:30,655
Hey, you're alive, right?
And that's 'cause of who?

483
00:25:30,696 --> 00:25:32,657
-You.
-No, not just me.

484
00:25:32,698 --> 00:25:34,659
If Sweeney hadn't gone
to Castellano, you'd be dead,

485
00:25:34,700 --> 00:25:36,202
so don't forget that.

486
00:25:36,244 --> 00:25:38,579
If he wants us to do a job,
we do it.

487
00:25:38,621 --> 00:25:42,166
He's the fuckin' boss.
Not you. Not me.

488
00:25:44,126 --> 00:25:46,003
[doorbell jingling]

489
00:25:52,635 --> 00:25:53,886
Hello, Finn.

490
00:25:55,012 --> 00:25:56,764
Boys. How may I help you?

491
00:25:56,806 --> 00:25:58,557
You know why we're here.

492
00:25:58,599 --> 00:26:01,686
Uh, Mr. Sweeney will have
his money by next Tuesday.

493
00:26:01,727 --> 00:26:04,021
Yeah, you said that
last Tuesday.

494
00:26:04,063 --> 00:26:06,399
[Finn] I meant
the Tuesday after this.

495
00:26:06,440 --> 00:26:07,275
[Mickey]
What you got there?

496
00:26:09,235 --> 00:26:10,945
These fuckin' dog tags?

497
00:26:10,987 --> 00:26:12,989
Are you selling these?

498
00:26:13,030 --> 00:26:15,324
You can put your name
on the blank ones.

499
00:26:15,366 --> 00:26:16,867
Yeah, I got some already.

500
00:26:17,868 --> 00:26:19,578
So do my buddies,

501
00:26:19,620 --> 00:26:21,455
half of them lyin'
in a fucking jungle right now!

502
00:26:21,497 --> 00:26:23,499
-You fucking cocksucker!
-Hey, hey, hey.

503
00:26:23,541 --> 00:26:24,917
Calm down.
All right?

504
00:26:26,335 --> 00:26:28,129
Look, look,

505
00:26:28,170 --> 00:26:30,006
my bookie ran off
with my money.

506
00:26:30,047 --> 00:26:32,591
You shouldn't be betting
on the fuckin' horses, Finn.

507
00:26:32,633 --> 00:26:34,176
Do you remember
what I said last time?

508
00:26:34,218 --> 00:26:35,761
-[Finn] Yeah.
-No money,

509
00:26:35,803 --> 00:26:37,555
I'm gonna have
to break your thumbs.

510
00:26:37,596 --> 00:26:39,348
Or I'm gonna cut 'em off
