the bartender at the 596

765
00:39:12,768 --> 00:39:14,144
he's gonna
put a bullet in Danny

766
00:39:14,186 --> 00:39:15,437
I don't get him out
of the Kitchen.

767
00:39:15,479 --> 00:39:17,814
Let me be clear
on what you're asking me.

768
00:39:17,856 --> 00:39:19,316
You want me
to arrest your son?

769
00:39:19,357 --> 00:39:21,234
No. I can position that.

770
00:39:21,276 --> 00:39:23,195
What I need from you is
to use your influence

771
00:39:23,236 --> 00:39:24,863
with the authorities
to get him out of town.

772
00:39:24,905 --> 00:39:26,990
You're asking me
to use federal pull

773
00:39:27,032 --> 00:39:30,160
to ship your kid to a safe house
disguised as a clinic?

774
00:39:30,202 --> 00:39:32,204
Yeah, won't look good
if the son

775
00:39:32,245 --> 00:39:34,247
of one of your informants
turns up in the East River.

776
00:39:35,665 --> 00:39:37,334
What do I get?

777
00:39:37,375 --> 00:39:40,045
I think there's a connection
between Sweeney, Castellano,

778
00:39:40,087 --> 00:39:42,130
and that fire
at the Starship disco.

779
00:39:42,172 --> 00:39:43,673
Got any proof?

780
00:39:43,715 --> 00:39:46,718
I'm workin' on it.
But not if I'm burying my kid.

781
00:39:47,886 --> 00:39:51,098
Location I can't promise,
but I'll see what I can do.

782
00:39:51,139 --> 00:39:53,683
You fuck me on this,
I'll let the kid rot.

783
00:39:54,935 --> 00:39:56,269
I owe you.

784
00:39:56,311 --> 00:39:57,771
Yeah, you do.

785
00:39:57,813 --> 00:40:00,232
[rock music playing]

786
00:40:02,818 --> 00:40:04,152
You're too fucking
trustin', Jimmy.

787
00:40:04,194 --> 00:40:05,112
Fuck off.

788
00:40:08,949 --> 00:40:11,493
Problem is, you put
Sweeney on a pedestal.

789
00:40:11,535 --> 00:40:14,621
We all did, but now we know
he don't fuckin' belong there.

790
00:40:14,663 --> 00:40:16,039
What are you,
a fuckin' shrink now?

791
00:40:16,081 --> 00:40:17,707
Well, you ain't gotta be
a fuckin' shrink, Jimmy.

792
00:40:17,749 --> 00:40:20,585
Any idiot can see that this
motherfucker is out for himself.

793
00:40:20,627 --> 00:40:22,712
I just can't believe
I couldn't see it before.

794
00:40:22,754 --> 00:40:24,965
But now, we got to accept it.

795
00:40:27,008 --> 00:40:28,927
Look, brother, I get it.

796
00:40:28,969 --> 00:40:30,512
Right, the guy's done
a lot for you.

797
00:40:31,555 --> 00:40:33,682
After what happened with
your mother, taking you in,

798
00:40:33,723 --> 00:40:35,517
putting a roof over your head,
that's not nothing.

799
00:40:35,559 --> 00:40:37,227
And what? I'm not supposed
to be fuckin' grateful for that?

800
00:40:39,312 --> 00:40:41,064
Sure.

801
00:40:41,106 --> 00:40:43,191
But understand it
for what it is.

802
00:40:43,233 --> 00:40:44,985
He has your loyalty, right?

803
00:40:45,026 --> 00:40:47,070
You would die for
that motherfucker. I know you.

804
00:40:47,112 --> 00:40:49,156
You think
he'd say the same for you?

805
00:40:49,197 --> 00:40:51,366
He wouldn't,
and he never will.

806
00:40:52,284 --> 00:40:53,577
-I can't believe that.
-Jimmy,

807
00:40:53,618 --> 00:40:55,162
the guy showed us
who he is.

808
00:40:55,203 --> 00:40:57,831
He's a fuckin' criminal,
through and through.

809
00:40:57,873 --> 00:41:01,001
He pretends he's some fancy
fuckin' do-gooder, you know,

810
00:41:01,042 --> 00:41:03,628
walking around in his suits
and bowin' to old ladies,

811
00:41:03,670 --> 00:41:05,380
givin' his speeches
about the neighborhood,

812
00:41:05,422 --> 00:41:06,756
telling everybody
and their mother,

813
00:41:06,798 --> 00:41:08,341
oh, no,
we don't sell narcotics.

814
00:41:08,383 --> 00:41:10,343
No, that's not in our streets,
that's a dirty business.

815
00:41:10,385 --> 00:41:12,053
But then what does he do?

816
00:41:12,095 --> 00:41:14,055
He sells our product
and uses the money for himself,

817
00:41:14,097 --> 00:41:16,057
it makes me fuckin' sick!

818
00:41:17,100 --> 00:41:19,019
I just can't believe
he lied to my fuckin' face.

819
00:41:19,060 --> 00:41:21,188
Right, but he did.

820
00:41:21,229 --> 00:41:22,606
Jimmy, this is
the same motherfucker

821
00:41:22,647 --> 00:41:24,274
that killed Davey O'Brien,

822
00:41:24,316 --> 00:41:26,109
and he wanted you
to shoot me.

823
00:41:26,151 --> 00:41:27,277
And you know what?

824
00:41:29,029 --> 00:41:30,572
I haven't heard shit about Pat

825
00:41:30,614 --> 00:41:32,073
since he said
he was lookin' into it.

826
00:41:33,575 --> 00:41:35,160
I'm just saying,

827
00:41:35,202 --> 00:41:36,995
now we know
that this motherfucker

828
00:41:37,037 --> 00:41:38,371
ain't one of us.

829
00:41:41,124 --> 00:41:43,293
So what am I supposed to do?

830
00:41:43,335 --> 00:41:44,461
Hmm?

831
00:41:46,379 --> 00:41:48,048
You know,
what if we're wrong?

832
00:41:49,257 --> 00:41:51,218
What if he didn't sell the coke?
He just-- He just donated

833
00:41:51,259 --> 00:41:52,886
that money from his--
from his savings.

834
00:41:52,928 --> 00:41:54,179
[scoffs]

835
00:41:54,221 --> 00:41:56,014
Right...

836
00:41:56,056 --> 00:41:57,599
and I hear there's
a bridge in Brooklyn for sale.

837
00:42:02,312 --> 00:42:05,482
You know, you got a heart
of fuckin' gold, Jimmy.

838
00:42:06,858 --> 00:42:09,361
Don't ever lose that. Please.

839
00:42:10,654 --> 00:42:11,988
But don't give it
to a motherfucker

840
00:42:12,030 --> 00:42:13,490
who don't deserve it either.

841
00:42:16,618 --> 00:42:18,161
Where're you going?

842
00:42:18,203 --> 00:42:19,955
I'm going
to that fuckin' dinner.

843
00:42:19,996 --> 00:42:21,456
And I'm gonna make him
tell me the fuckin' truth.

844
00:42:21,498 --> 00:42:22,540
[loud slam]

845
00:42:48,775 --> 00:42:51,152
[Glenn]
Jacob's Biscuits.

846
00:42:51,194 --> 00:42:52,529
He's in his room.

847
00:43:00,161 --> 00:43:02,872
[rock music playing
through headphones]

848
00:43:04,332 --> 00:43:05,834
Hey! Hey!

849
00:43:05,875 --> 00:43:07,752
Take those fuckin' things off.

850
00:43:08,962 --> 00:43:10,547
-What the hell do you want?
-What are you doing

851
00:43:10,588 --> 00:43:12,299
hanging around with Sweeney?
You shouldn't be doing that.

852
00:43:12,340 --> 00:43:13,633
What, does that
make you nervous?

853
00:43:13,675 --> 00:43:15,302
I understand he told you
to stay away from him.

854
00:43:17,637 --> 00:43:19,139
You honestly expect me
to believe that bullshit

855
00:43:19,180 --> 00:43:21,016
you were spilling
the other day?

856
00:43:21,057 --> 00:43:23,184
About how some Puerto Rican guy
who killed Pat Murphy?

857
00:43:23,226 --> 00:43:24,477
Oh, he magically gets killed

858
00:43:24,519 --> 00:43:25,562
after you beat
the shit out of me!

859
00:43:25,603 --> 00:43:27,105
Oh, what? You think

860
00:43:27,147 --> 00:43:28,732
-Sweeney and I killed Pat?
-Who cares?

861
00:43:28,773 --> 00:43:30,984
-I just want my job back!
-You're playin' with fire!

862
00:43:32,193 --> 00:43:33,320
I'm tryin' to protect you!

863
00:43:33,361 --> 00:43:34,696
I can take care of myself!

864
00:43:34,738 --> 00:43:36,865
No, you can't!
In fact, I know you can't!

865
00:43:36,906 --> 00:43:38,700
Leave me alone, and stay
the fuck out of my life!

866
00:43:38,742 --> 00:43:40,577
Yeah, okay.

867
00:43:40,618 --> 00:43:41,911
All right, tough guy.

868
00:43:45,081 --> 00:43:46,291
What's this?

869
00:43:46,333 --> 00:43:47,917
Hmm?

870
00:43:47,959 --> 00:43:49,085
What, are you
selling this shit?

871
00:43:49,127 --> 00:43:50,462
Or you just using it?

872
00:43:50,503 --> 00:43:52,881
What the fuck are you doing?
That's not mine!

873
00:43:52,922 --> 00:43:54,174
You know what?

874
00:43:56,051 --> 00:43:58,470
One day, you're gonna
thank me for this.

875
00:43:58,511 --> 00:43:59,888
Fuck you!

876
00:43:59,929 --> 00:44:02,599
[tense music]

877
00:44:27,248 --> 00:44:28,500
Any chatter?

878
00:44:28,541 --> 00:44:29,709
Not yet.

879
00:44:36,841 --> 00:44:38,426
I want you
to meet the others.

880
00:44:38,468 --> 00:44:39,552
Mary!

881
00:44:43,306 --> 00:44:46,518
Now, you've all heard
of the girl in the grey coat.

882
00:44:46,559 --> 00:44:48,311
Now you're lookin' at her.

883
00:44:48,353 --> 00:44:50,063
This is Sarah McKenna,

884
00:44:50,105 --> 00:44:52,440
AKA Bridget Walsh.

885
00:44:52,482 --> 00:44:54,776
This is
Tadhg McKenna's daughter.

886
00:44:54,818 --> 00:44:56,611
Now, she's currently called
Bridget Walsh because of

887
00:44:56,653 --> 00:44:59,072
the Interpol warrant
that bears her name

888
00:44:59,114 --> 00:45:00,657
for the bombings
of the London Tube.

889
00:45:01,783 --> 00:45:03,201
She's a hero.

890
00:45:04,661 --> 00:45:07,080
This here's Logan,
you'll remember him.

891
00:45:07,122 --> 00:45:09,916
He's a history teacher from
Boston, long-time sympathizer.

892
00:45:09,958 --> 00:45:11,292
I have family in Belfast.

893
00:45:11,334 --> 00:45:13,044
It's an honor to meet you.

894
00:45:13,086 --> 00:45:14,838
And that's Donal,
who you've met.

895
00:45:14,879 --> 00:45:17,215
He's from Derry.
He came over with me.

896
00:45:17,257 --> 00:45:19,759
He's an explosive expert,
apparently.

897
00:45:19,801 --> 00:45:21,386
Careful there, Donal.

898
00:45:21,428 --> 00:45:24,389
As long as nobody sneezes,
I'm all right.

899
00:45:24,431 --> 00:45:25,598
Cheers, Bridget.

900
00:45:26,558 --> 00:45:28,893
That's Mary.
She's from Hell's Kitchen.

901
00:45:28,935 --> 00:45:31,104
I've seen you speak at NORAID.

902
00:45:31,146 --> 00:45:32,522
Is she joining us?

903
00:45:33,481 --> 00:45:35,900
To Mary's point...

904
00:45:35,942 --> 00:45:37,527
they've all taken the oath

905
00:45:37,569 --> 00:45:39,863
of loyalty
to the Irish Republican Army.

906
00:45:39,904 --> 00:45:41,322
Any objections?

907
00:45:43,158 --> 00:45:44,742
The loyalty oath.

908
00:45:47,078 --> 00:45:48,496
Yeah, I know it well.

909
00:45:49,914 --> 00:45:52,125
Do you have a gun
and a Bible handy?

910
00:45:52,167 --> 00:45:53,585
Yeah, we do.

911
00:45:58,381 --> 00:46:00,884
[tense music]

912
00:46:00,925 --> 00:46:02,260
[officer]
Come on. Let's go.

913
00:46:03,261 --> 00:46:04,679
Move.

914
00:46:08,391 --> 00:46:09,684
Watch your head.

915
00:46:14,522 --> 00:46:16,399
-Appreciate it.
-[car door shutting]

916
00:46:20,195 --> 00:46:23,615
Moira, don't worry.
It's what's best for the boy.

917
00:46:27,785 --> 00:46:29,245
Guess she's not
a fan of yours.

918
00:46:46,012 --> 00:46:47,931
-[applause]
-Thank you.

919
00:46:50,266 --> 00:46:51,809
This is very humbling.

920
00:46:51,851 --> 00:46:53,019
Wow, 1980.

921
00:46:54,395 --> 00:46:55,563
Time flies.

922
00:46:57,065 --> 00:46:58,566
Especially you get
to be my age.

923
00:46:58,608 --> 00:47:00,985
[crowd laughing]

924
00:47:02,654 --> 00:47:03,696
[clears throat]

925
00:47:05,990 --> 00:47:08,243
My father left me
two things...

926
00:47:08,284 --> 00:47:10,578
that are
very important to me.

927
00:47:10,620 --> 00:47:12,330
His rosary...

928
00:47:12,372 --> 00:47:13,998
and a debt

929
00:47:14,040 --> 00:47:16,334
that I never got to repay...

930
00:47:16,376 --> 00:47:17,794
until tonight.

931
00:47:18,920 --> 00:47:21,047
That debt was not money.

932
00:47:21,089 --> 00:47:23,258
It was the price of keepin'
our name outta the gutter

933
00:47:23,299 --> 00:47:25,260
and our heads above the water.

934
00:47:25,301 --> 00:47:27,971
I, Sarah McKenna,

935
00:47:28,012 --> 00:47:30,181
AKA Bridget Walsh,

936
00:47:30,223 --> 00:47:31,683
do solemnly swear

937
00:47:31,724 --> 00:47:33,142
in the presence
of Almighty God

938
00:47:33,184 --> 00:47:34,435
and my comrades in arms

939
00:47:34,477 --> 00:47:36,563
to uphold and protect

940
00:47:36,604 --> 00:47:38,022
the Irish Republican Army

941
00:47:38,064 --> 00:47:41,234
with all that I have
and all I may ever be.

942
00:47:41,276 --> 00:47:43,319
[Sweeney]
It's been paid by bricklayers

943
00:47:43,361 --> 00:47:45,280
who drank their pain,

944
00:47:45,321 --> 00:47:47,740
by proud Irish mothers

945
00:47:47,782 --> 00:47:49,576
who scrubbed
other people's floors

946
00:47:49,617 --> 00:47:52,161
so their sons wouldn't
have to steal.

947
00:47:52,203 --> 00:47:55,456
It's been paid
in favors and funerals.

948
00:47:55,498 --> 00:47:57,792
In silence...

949
00:47:57,834 --> 00:47:59,961
and in fists.

950
00:48:00,003 --> 00:48:01,838
In blood
we never bragged about.

951
00:48:03,381 --> 00:48:04,882
We built this neighborhood.

952
00:48:06,301 --> 00:48:08,428
And, yeah, we bled for it.

953
00:48:08,469 --> 00:48:11,055
And we buried
more than a few good souls

954
00:48:11,097 --> 00:48:13,474
to make sure we hold onto it.

955
00:48:13,516 --> 00:48:16,853
I pledge obedience
without question

956
00:48:16,894 --> 00:48:18,521
to follow commands,

957
00:48:18,563 --> 00:48:20,565
to carry out justice,

958
00:48:20,607 --> 00:48:22,275
to keep the secrets
of this cause

959
00:48:22,317 --> 00:48:24,527
until my last breath

960
00:48:24,569 --> 00:48:27,155
or until
Ireland stands whole.

961
00:48:27,196 --> 00:48:28,698
[Sweeney]
And we did it with pride

962
00:48:28,740 --> 00:48:30,950
because we belong.

963
00:48:31,618 --> 00:48:33,620
Tonight, we remember
who we are.

964
00:48:33,661 --> 00:48:35,622
And who we will never be.

965
00:48:35,663 --> 00:48:37,498
We're not some
forgotten little tribe

966
00:48:37,540 --> 00:48:39,459
in a tiny corner of Manhattan.

967
00:48:39,500 --> 00:48:42,045
We Irish are its spine.

968
00:48:42,086 --> 00:48:44,672
[Bridget]
I swear to fight, to suffer,

969
00:48:44,714 --> 00:48:46,924
and, if called, to die...

970
00:48:48,301 --> 00:48:51,220
...for the dream
of a United Ireland.

971
00:48:51,262 --> 00:48:52,972
Until the tricolor
flies in peace

972
00:48:53,014 --> 00:48:55,725
from Belfast to Derry,
or I lie beneath it.

973
00:48:55,767 --> 00:48:57,143
So help me God.

974
00:48:57,185 --> 00:48:59,187
[Sweeney]
When I say thank you tonight,

975
00:48:59,228 --> 00:49:01,939
I'm talking not only
about this lovely award.

976
00:49:01,981 --> 00:49:03,399
[speaking Gaelic]

977
00:49:03,441 --> 00:49:05,318
[Sweeney]
I'm talking about a legacy.

978
00:49:05,360 --> 00:49:07,904
The kind you don't hang
on the wall,

979
00:49:07,945 --> 00:49:10,073
a legacy you carry
in your heart.

980
00:49:12,200 --> 00:49:14,452
It's in your bones.

981
00:49:14,494 --> 00:49:16,871
And I promise you
right here and now,

982
00:49:16,913 --> 00:49:19,624
long as I'm breathing,

983
00:49:19,666 --> 00:49:21,250
nobody is gonna forget that

984
00:49:21,292 --> 00:49:24,128
we Irish built
this neighborhood!

985
00:49:24,170 --> 00:49:26,923
[cheering]

986
00:49:36,182 --> 00:49:38,184
[♪ House of the Rising Sun ♪
playing]

987
00:49:38,226 --> 00:49:41,229
♪ I got one foot ♪

988
00:49:41,270 --> 00:49:44,774
♪ On the platform ♪

989
00:49:48,444 --> 00:49:52,031
♪ And another one ♪

990
00:49:52,073 --> 00:49:56,452
♪ On the train ♪

991
00:49:58,371 --> 00:50:03,167
♪ I'm going home ♪

992
00:50:03,209 --> 00:50:08,589
♪ To New Orleans ♪

993
00:50:08,631 --> 00:50:11,092
♪ To wear ♪

994
00:50:11,134 --> 00:50:15,179
♪ That ball and chain ♪

995
00:50:16,889 --> 00:50:18,933
[gurgling]

996
00:50:24,480 --> 00:50:25,773
Looks like the Italians
weren't too happy

997
00:50:25,815 --> 00:50:27,233
with you selling that coke.

998
00:50:27,275 --> 00:50:28,901
[chuckles]

999
00:50:33,239 --> 00:50:34,574
Yeah.

1000
00:50:37,285 --> 00:50:38,453
You wanna get a beer?

1001
00:50:38,494 --> 00:50:42,999
♪ And it's been the ruin ♪

1002
00:50:43,040 --> 00:50:48,796
♪ Of many a poor boy ♪

1003
00:50:50,381 --> 00:50:53,593
♪ And God ♪

1004
00:50:53,634 --> 00:50:56,512
♪ I know ♪

1005
00:50:57,847 --> 00:51:02,727
♪ I'm one ♪

1006
00:51:06,189 --> 00:51:10,067
[♪ House of the Rising Sun ♪
continues]

1007
00:51:55,822 --> 00:51:58,157
Subtitling: difuze

1008
00:52:08,751 --> 00:52:12,922
[police siren]

